{"id":"b5","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":5,"of":9,"title":"What happened","titleHe":"זְמַן עָבָר","goal":"Use the past tense of pa'al, where every person has its own ending.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Unlike the present, the past marks person as well as gender — nine endings, hung on a stem that stays put. Because the ending already says who, the pronoun is often dropped: כָּתַבְתִּי on its own means I wrote."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פָּעַל","en":"pa'al (kal)","note":"The plain, basic verb — the one most everyday actions use.","verb":{"root":"כ־ת־ב","inf":"לִכְתֹּב","en":"to write"},"tense":"past","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"כָּתַבְתִּי"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"כָּתַבְתָּ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"כָּתַבְתְּ"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"כָּתַב"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"כָּתְבָה"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"כָּתַבְנוּ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּם"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּן"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"כָּתְבוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The third person masculine singular — כָּתַב — has no ending at all. That bare form is the dictionary form of every Hebrew verb, which is why dictionaries list wrote rather than to write."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל קָרָאתִי סֵפֶר.","en":"Yesterday I read a book."},{"he":"הֵם לָמְדוּ עִבְרִית.","en":"They studied Hebrew."},{"he":"לֹא שָׁמַעְתִּי.","en":"I didn't hear."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל","en":"yesterday","translit":"etmol"},{"he":"הָיָה","en":"was (m.)","translit":"haya"},{"he":"הָיְתָה","en":"was (f.)","translit":"hayta"},{"he":"אָמַר","en":"said","translit":"amar"},{"he":"בָּא","en":"came","translit":"ba"},{"he":"הָלַךְ","en":"went","translit":"halach"},{"he":"נָתַן","en":"gave","translit":"natan"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["yesterday","good","is finished","therefore"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֶתְמוֹל","translit":"etmol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["and he said","was (m.)","her","falls"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הָיָה","translit":"haya"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["actually","bad","was (f.)","feeling"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הָיְתָה","translit":"hayta"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["was born","girl","nobody","said"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אָמַר","translit":"amar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sees","don't (with the future)","already","came"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בָּא","translit":"ba"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["city","went","head","seems, looks"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הָלַךְ","translit":"halach"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hook","head","gave","certainly"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נָתַן","translit":"natan"},{"type":"choice","q":"write — they, past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתְבוּ"],"correct":3,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: they is כָּתְבוּ."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “went”?","options":["אוֹהֵב","גָּדוֹל","בֵּית סֵפֶר","הָלַךְ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — you (f.), past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַב"],"correct":0,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: you (f.) is כָּתַבְתְּ."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["נָתַן","אָמַר","אֶתְמוֹל","הָיָה"],"correct":1,"say":"אָמַר","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["הָיְתָה","was (f.)"],["אֶתְמוֹל","yesterday"],["נָתַן","gave"],["אָמַר","said"],["בָּא","came"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “gave”?","options":["כְּבָר","מִי","נָתַן","בַּיִת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — I, past","options":["כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַב","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתַבְתְּ"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: I is כָּתַבְתִּי."},{"type":"choice","q":"write — you (m.pl.), past","options":["כָּתַבְתָּ","כְּתַבְתֶּם","כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתִּי"],"correct":1,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: you (m.pl.) is כְּתַבְתֶּם."},{"type":"choice","q":"write — you (f.pl.), past","options":["כָּתַבְתָּ","כְּתַבְתֶּן","כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתִּי"],"correct":1,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: you (f.pl.) is כְּתַבְתֶּן."}]}